From 699bb0b811531b17b003f2f873edefa66d81fac3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Florian Kleber <26285351+kleberbaum@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 08:26:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] feat(bridge): send styled text that rust builds as a
 component

Every text of EssentialsX is coloured, and its texts are MiniMessage
with colours, decorations and links. The actions message and broadcast
carry plain text, so a port would have to write formatting codes into
its lines, which also pass on whatever codes a player put into a name,
and it could neither link a word nor show a line on a hover.

A plugin now builds a golem_bridge::Text in Rust: the words of the
plugin, what a player wrote or named, a translation, the colours and
decorations of the game, a click, a hover, an insertion and the texts
after it. The actions styledMessage and styledBroadcast carry its JSON,
the form that Component.Serializer of Minecraft reads, which the plugin
API names its text component, and the mod reads it as the game reads
the text of tellraw. What a player wrote or named stays literal: it is
a text of its own and loses every formatting code and control
character, so no player colours the rest of a line or starts one. The
JSON escapes every control character, so it never breaks the wire
form, and the context of a plugin refuses a text that the game could
not send a client or that nests deeper than 32. A styled broadcast
leaves out the players it hides, as the AFK and suicide notices of
EssentialsX leave out the players who ignore the sender.

The subcommand text-json of the devtool prints the JSON of described
texts for notebook 04, and the client of the harness reads the
components of the system messages it gets, so notebook 05 checks the
colour, the click and the hover that reach a player.

